Backport Windows support (ConPTY) from lxqt/qtermwidget PR #578

Vendored verbatim from the pull request, which is open and will stay that way.
It swaps the POSIX KPty stack for a ConPTY one on Windows: lib/ptyqt/ gains an
abstract IPtyProcess plus a ConPtyProcess implementation, Pty is reparented to
QObject instead of KPtyProcess, and CMake drops kpty.cpp/kptydevice.cpp/
kptyprocess.cpp/BlockArray.cpp from the Windows build. History moves off mmap
onto QTemporaryFile::map() and widens its offsets to qint64.

    PR:     https://github.com/lxqt/qtermwidget/pull/578
    Author: loliting, 2025-01-01, branch loliting:windows-support

Provenance of the vendored code, per the PR's own README additions:

    lib/ptyqt/conptyprocess.{h,cpp}  Vitaly Petrov <v31337@gmail.com>, MIT
    lib/ptyqt/iptyprocess.{h,cpp}    Waqar Ahmed <waqar.17a@gmail.com>, MIT
    lib/wcwidth.c                    Markus Kuhn, MIT

    upstream of ptyqt: https://github.com/kafeg/ptyqt

WHY THIS IS CARRIED DOWNSTREAM AND NOT WAITED ON

The PR is not blocked on technical review. The qtermwidget maintainer declined
it on the first day and again in June 2025, both times on manpower grounds:

    "LXQt doesn't have the required manpower to support Windows."
    "As the current maintainer of qterminal+qtermwidget, I don't (and won't)
     have Windows (to say nothing of the time)."
        -- tsujan, https://github.com/lxqt/qtermwidget/pull/578#issuecomment-2566430448

When another contributor offered to do the review, the answer was a flat "No":

    https://github.com/lxqt/qtermwidget/pull/578#issuecomment-2979012570

The author has said he does not need it upstreamed. So do not wait for this to
merge, and do not drop this patch on a version bump expecting upstream to have
taken it. Re-check the PR's state, then refresh the patch.

THE REST OF THE PAPER TRAIL

    #42   https://github.com/lxqt/qtermwidget/issues/42
          The original 2015 "Port qtermwidget to Windows" request. Closed with
          "PRs accepted, but we're not leaving a tracker bug open for this."
          Everything below cross-references it.
    #240  https://github.com/lxqt/qtermwidget/issues/240
          GNU Octave maintains an independent fork with win32 support, a second
          prior-art lineage if this one ever goes stale:
          https://hg.savannah.gnu.org/hgweb/octave/file/tip/libgui/qterminal/libqterminal/
    #491  https://github.com/lxqt/qtermwidget/issues/491
    #494  https://github.com/lxqt/qtermwidget/issues/494
          Two later "is there a Windows plan?" reports, both closed as no.

    KangLin's fork, which tracks the PR and asked for CI:
          https://github.com/KangLin/qtermwidget

KNOWN GAPS -- none of these are regressions this patch introduces, but they are
what is still wrong after it:

  - startTerminalTeletype() / Session::runEmptyPTY() is reported non-working on
    Windows and the report is unanswered:
    https://github.com/lxqt/qtermwidget/pull/578#issuecomment-3009278241
    ConPTY has no pty-without-a-process concept, so there is nothing obvious for
    setEmptyPTYProperties() to do. Public API that silently does nothing.
  - Character::character is a wchar_t, 16 bits on Windows, so every code point
    above the BMP is truncated before it reaches the renderer. Making the
    terminal actually run only makes this visible. See 0002 for the narrow part
    of it that could be fixed cheaply.
  - No Windows CI exists upstream or in the fork (KangLin's runs ubuntu-20.04),
    and nothing here had been built with mingw-w64 before this package did it.

Upstream: submitted as PR #578 by its author; declined for maintenance reasons
Applies-to: all environments (inert off Windows -- every hunk is behind WIN32)

